2026-09-05 13:30:27 ERROR [__main__] install failed: WoW TBC in C:\gate\tbc-server was built before this app carried shared/cmangos/patches/vmap-extractor-doodad-name-case.patch, and this press would skip the compile: the build is recorded and its images are still here. Patching the source now would leave the checkout holding a fix that the built server does not have and cannot get, because the extractor runs from the image and the maps it already wrote would not be rebuilt either. Nothing was changed, and the server you have goes on working exactly as it did. To get the fix, keep this folder and take away what this press would skip: use “Stop and remove containers…” on the Server tab, then `docker image rm yulon.local/cmangos-tbc-server:native-8cce6242` and delete C:\gate\tbc-server\data\.yulon-extract.json and C:\gate\tbc-server\data\Buildings, then install again into the same folder with the same client. That recompiles the server and extracts the maps a second time, which takes hours, and it leaves the install folder, its database and the characters in it alone. C:\gate\tbc-server\data\Buildings goes with it because the extractor refuses to start into a folder that already holds dir or dir_bin; a press that leaves it there stops there instead. That folder holds an extraction this app made, not anything of yours, and deleting it is what a second extraction needs: the tool writes it from the client again, which takes tens of minutes and touches nothing else under data/. Do not delete C:\gate\tbc-server instead: .db_password is inside it and is the only copy of the password this install's database volume yulon-wow-tbc-8cce6242_db-data was created with. Removing the containers keeps that volume, so a fresh install into the same folder would stop for a lost password, and the only way past that stop deletes the volume and every character in it.
